data: {"text": "Here are **real, non‑AI photos of Mount Everest** and its surroundings from reputable sources (not generated images). These include the summit, the base camp, and Himalayan landscapes captured by photographers and published online. \n\n### 📸 Real Everest Photos\n**Mountain & Summit Views**\n- **Everest summit and surrounding ridges** — dramatic, high‑altitude views of the iconic peak. (Getty Images)   \n- **View from Kala Patthar** — Everest nestled among its Himalayan neighbors. (Getty Images)   \n- **Snowy slopes & crags** — close‑up of Everest’s rugged terrain. (Getty Images)   \n- **Dusk light on Everest** — atmospheric alpine light and shadows. (Getty Images)   \n- **Peak from different angle** — alternative perspective of Everest’s summit massif. (Getty Images)   \n- **Panoramic Himalayan landscape** — Everest and adjacent peaks in context. (iStock via Getty) \n\n**Base Camp & Expedition Scenes**\n- **Everest Base Camp on Khumbu Glacier** — tents and gear at high altitude, showing how climbers prepare before ascents.   \n  *Example:* **Everest Base Camp tents & terrain** — expedition infrastructure at ~5,300 m. (Getty Images)   \n- **Panoramic Base Camp view** — glacier, tents, and Himalayan peaks in one frame. (Getty Images) \n\n---\n\n### 📌 Sources for These *Real* Photos\nYou can explore additional legitimate photos of Mount Everest from these well‑known photo and editorial collections:\n\n**Photo galleries & editorial sources**\n- **National Geographic Everest galleries** — curated photography from real expeditions to Mount Everest and base camp.   \n- **Pexels & Pixabay free photo repositories** — thousands of user‑submitted Everest photos (landscapes, base camp, mountain views).   \n- **Wikimedia Commons** — archive of real summit and expedition images.   \n- **Getty Images & iStock collections** — professional high‑resolution photos of Everest landscapes and climbing scenes. \n\nIf you want **direct clickable photo galleries or high‑resolution downloads**, let me know whether you prefer *expedition history*, *base camp scenes*, or *summit panoramas*, and I can send you direct links to the best collections."}

